      "content": "I see. You noted that Sterling's work feels more \"established\" because of the complex modeling, while Adeyemi's seems more localized/descriptive. Could you expand on that? Specifically, when looking at the authors themselves, do you think the perceived authority of these papers is tied to the scale of their research focus, or is there something else in the way the findings are framed that makes Sterling's work seem more authoritative by default?",
